\title{Lamps in a hotel}
\language{en}
\range{-5..5}
\author{Gang XIAO}
\email{xiao@unice.fr}
\computeanswer{yes}
\format{html}
\precision{1000000}

\integer{lamps=random(10..20)}
\integer{eteints=random(2..4)}
\integer{distr=binomial(\lamps-\eteints-1,\eteints)}
\statement{A hotel has a long corridor lit by \lamps aligned lamps.
In order to save energy, the hotel turns off \eteints of these lamps
during the night. <p>
To have a minimum of lighting, one cannot turn off adjacent lamps, nor
lamps at the extremities of the corridor. In this case, how many different
ways there are to turn off \eteints lamps?}

\answer{Number of ways}{\distr}

